        "objective": "Shared-memory source tiling, one target per thread",
        "role": "T1",
        "subject": "Explore staging source positions and mass in shared memory in source chunks so multiple target threads reuse each staged source. Keep the output mapping at one target per thread to distinguish this from register-blocked output work. Tune a valid block/items_per_block/shared_memory_bytes configuration and the shared tile layout; handle partial source and target tiles without letting inactive threads skip required barriers. Preserve i==j exclusion, the exact interface and all correctness requirements. Compare using the prescribed three-size geometric-mean kernel-time objective, and retain only candidates that pass the full correctness checks."
      },
      {
        "objective": "Register-blocked target outputs",
        "role": "T2",
        "subject": "Explore assigning a small batch of target particles to each thread, with separate accumulators, so a source particle's loaded position and mass can be reused across those targets. This is an output-axis/register-reuse investigation, not merely another one-target-per-thread shared-memory tile. Tune the batch size and allowed launch configuration while monitoring register pressure and available parallelism. Cover all target tails and preserve the full state, self exclusion, numerical requirements, and exact masses. Measure against the prescribed objective and validate every candidate with the complete oracle/check suite."
      },
