        "objective": "Per-interaction arithmetic efficiency",
        "role": "T3",
        "subject": "Explore lowering the cost of pair evaluation while retaining the one-target-per-thread mapping as a clear comparison: for example, algebraically cancel target mass in the acceleration expression and evaluate inverse distance with rsqrtf to form an inverse-cube factor. Test arithmetic ordering and only consider FMA or loop unrolling when measurements justify them. These transformations change floating-point rounding: preserve softening and self exclusion, use no global fast-math option, and reject any candidate that fails tolerances, oracle checks, or the nonfinite-output constraint, including extreme-mass and coincident-position cases. Compare on the official geometric-mean metric."
      }
